    "id": "339148807",
    "body": "**Review: Proposed Tag-Based Environment Promotion (GitFlow)**\n\n**Findings**\n\n1. **Tag-permission model can't be enforced as described.** \"Any developer creates `-rc` tags, only tier-1-approvers create final/hotfix tags\" is specified as a single GitHub Ruleset targeting `v*`. Confirmed against GitHub's own docs: one bypass list applies to everything a ruleset's target pattern matches — there's no way for one ruleset to grant open access to one sub-pattern while restricting another. This needs two rulesets in the design itself.\n2. **SIT's tag-based promotion isn't actually specified.** The proposal states SIT gets \"re-deployed only when a new `-rc` is cut,\" but `deploy-sit.yml`'s real trigger (`workflow_run` off the SIT Gate passing on a release-branch push) has no relationship to tag creation — it fires on every push to the branch regardless of tags. This needs an explicit decision: make SIT tag-triggered (a real design change), or keep it branch-triggered and stop describing it as tag-scoped.\n3. **Existing tagging tooling is left unaddressed.**`scripts/tagRelease.sh` is what the current Branching Guide already prescribes for tagging, and it conflicts with what's proposed here (different tool, different tag format, different point in the flow). Separately, `tag-sprint` (in `deploy-dev.yml`) and the Confluence-described `tag-sit-deploy` job already produce tags in their own namespace. Worth stating what happens to both.\n4. **A dependency this proposal relies on, owned elsewhere.***Environment Topology & Promotion Path*'s environment table lists `staging`/`pre-prod`/`production`; live GitHub state is `dev, staging, sit, test, uat, prod` (no `pre-prod`, no `production`), and `staging` is actually Stage's environment, not Dev's. The version-guard this proposal introduces depends on this mapping being correct.\n\n**Work to take note of***(ordinary follow-on once approved, not evidence of anything wrong)*\n\n* Once SIT's design (finding 2) is decided, `deploy-sit.yml` will need a corresponding code change.\n* `semver` isn't a declared dependency yet — normal approval applies once the version-guard is actually built.\n* The Test-gate design depends on the Test tier's own secrets/config (already tracked separately) landing first.\n\n**Open questions**\n\n1. **Test gate design → deploy-then-gate.** SIT's own gate-then-deploy doesn't test the artifact being promoted — its Playwright job has no build/deploy step and points at a static, pre-existing URL, since the gate runs before `deploy-sit` fires. Deploy-then-gate for Test tests the real, just-deployed build and keeps the fast on-demand \"quick look\" that's the point of this tier.\n2. **Test gate scope → P0 Playwright + bundle-size only.** Bundle-size is cheap and already wired, and supports the project's explicit mobile-performance priority. Contract-tests is a no-op stub regardless of tier. Lighthouse needs its own secrets that aren't even finished for SIT yet, and its trend-based value doesn't suit Test's disposable feature-branch use case.",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "title": "Re: Proposed: Tag-Based Environment Promotion (GitFlow)",
    "author": "Marcel Angelo Navarro",
    "location": "footer"
  }
]"}

