    "version": 22,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nIn a headless SFCC architecture the storefront presentation layer runs independently of the Salesforce Commerce Cloud backend. The SFCC platform is responsible exclusively for:\n\n* Business logic (pricing, promotions, tax, inventory)\n* Order management and checkout orchestration\n* Catalog management via Business Manager\n* Cartridge-based custom logic exposed through SCAPI / OCAPI\n\n**Scope of this document:** This page covers the SFCC-side build and deployment only — cartridge packaging, WebDAV upload, code version activation, Business Manager configuration, and data import/export. Frontend (Next.js / PWA Kit) deployment is documented separately — see PWA CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions).\n\n---\n\nSFCC deployment activities\n--------------------------\n\n1. **Developer commit:** SFCC cartridge code, metadata, jobs, services, hooks, and site-specific configuration changes are committed to the agreed source repository.\n2. **CI build:** The pipeline validates the cartridge structure, runs linting/unit checks, installs dependencies, and produces a deployable cartridge bundle.\n3. **Install vendor cartridges:**`npm run vendor:install` copies third-party cartridges from `vendor/` into `cartridges/` before packaging.\n4. **Package cartridges:** All cartridges in `cartridges/` are zipped in the required cartridge path order for the target SFCC instance.\n5. **Deploy to sandbox or development:** The package is uploaded to the SFCC instance using WebDAV or the approved deployment automation.\n6. **Activate code version:** A new code version is created or updated in Business Manager, then activated for validation.\n7. **Import configuration and data:** Required site preferences, custom objects, metadata, jobs, services, promotions, catalog, inventory, price book, and content changes are imported as applicable.\n8. **Rebuild search index:** After any data import the `RebuildALLSearchIndex` job is triggered automatically to ensure product search reflects the latest catalog state across all sites.\n9. **Validate SFCC functionality:** QA confirms cartridge behavior, Business Manager configuration, API responses, checkout flows, payment integrations, tax, shipping, promotions, and order export behavior.\n10. **Promote through environments:** The same validated package and configuration set moves through QA, Staging, and Production following approval gates.\n11. **Production release:** The production code version is activated, final imports are completed, smoke tests are run, and rollback readiness is confirmed.\n\n---\n\nEnvironment progression\n-----------------------\n\n| Stage | SFCC ENV | Purpose | Primary outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Local | Sandboxes | Developer local feature validation | Specific feature and story |\n| Development | BKZK-002 | Initial deployment and technical verification | Confirm package integrity and baseline functionality |\n| TEST | BKZK-005 | Initial deployment and technical verification | Confirm package integrity and baseline functionality |\n| SIT | BKZK-003 | Functional and regression validation | Integration readiness |\n| UAT | DEV-AP01 | Functional and regression validation | Verify business behavior and integration readiness |\n| Staging | STG-AP01 | Pre-production validation in a production-like setup | Support final business and release checks |\n| Production | PROD-AP01 | Live customer-facing deployment | Activate the approved backend code version |\n\n---\n\nRepository and cartridge structure\n----------------------------------\n\nnonezimmermann-sfcc/\n├── cartridges/\n│ ├── int\\_custom\\_zim\\_global/ # Zimmermann — global integrations & job steps\n│ ├── plugin\\_zim\\_scapi/ # Zimmermann — SCAPI / OCAPI hook overrides\n│ ├── int\\_globale/ # Global-e (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_globale\\_headless/ # Global-e headless (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_avatax\\_svcclient/ # Avalara AvaTax service client (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_avatax\\_sfra/ # Avalara AvaTax SFRA (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ └── bm\\_avatax/ # Avalara AvaTax BM extension (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n├── vendor/ # Third-party packages — source of truth (protected)\n│ ├── VENDORS.md # Upgrade runbook and package inventory\n│ ├── globale-v24.5.0/ # Full Global-e package + vendor.config.json\n│ └── avatax-v24.1.0/ # Full Avalara AvaTax package + vendor.config.json\n├── scripts/\n│ └── vendor-install.js # Reads vendor.config.json files, copies cartridges\n├── data/\n│ ├── core/ # Baseline data — imported to all envs\n│ └── sample/ # Dev/demo data — imported manually\n├── docs/ # Project documentation\n├── .github/\n│ ├── CODEOWNERS # vendor/ protected by @mani060689\n│ └── workflows/ # CI/CD pipeline definitions\n├── .env.example # Environment variable template\n├── package.json # Scripts, workspace config, Jest config\n└── build/ # Generated — gitignored\n> **Note:** Vendor cartridges under `cartridges/` are gitignored and generated at build time by `npm run vendor:install`. Never edit them directly — make changes in `vendor/` instead.\n>\n> **Note:** The `vendor/` folder requires approval from @mani060689 before any PR can be merged.\n\n### Adding or upgrading a vendor cartridge\n\n1. Download the new version zip from the vendor source.\n2. Create `vendor/<package>-v<version>/` and extract the zip into it.\n3. Add a `vendor.config.json` (copy from the previous version, update paths and version number).\n4. Delete the old version folder and update `vendor/VENDORS.md`.\n5. Run `npm run vendor:install` to apply changes locally.\n6. Commit `vendor/` changes together with any `data/` and `docs/` additions.\n\n---\n\nData and metadata deployment\n----------------------------\n\nData deployments are handled separately from code. They use SFCC's Site Archive (impex) mechanism and run as a distinct pipeline stage or manual job.\n\nThis data deployment does not apply to production since it is handled via Replication. Each code or data deployment is packaged and versioned and added to GitHub artifacts for promotion to environments.\n\n<https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/whiteboard/265256967>\n\n---\n\nGitHub Actions workflows\n------------------------\n\nThe repository contains five workflow files under `.github/workflows/`. Together they cover every stage of the development lifecycle from pull request through to staging.\n\n### Workflow overview\n\n| File | Name | Trigger | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `ci.yml` | CI | Push to `develop`, `feature/**`, `bugfix/**`, `hotfix/**`, `release/**`; PR to `main` or `develop` | Lint, unit tests (90% coverage threshold), XML schema validation |\n| `pr-check.yml` | PR Check | PR to `develop` or `main` | Quality gate — tests with coverage, posts coverage comment on the PR |\n| `cd-deploy.yml` | CD — Deploy (dev / SIT) | Push to `develop`; manual `workflow_dispatch` | Deploy code and data to Development (BKZK-002) or SIT (BKZK-003) |\n| `cd-test.yml` | CD — Test (scheduled) | Scheduled twice daily at 7am and 7pm AEST; manual `workflow_dispatch` | Full refresh of TEST (BKZK-005) — code, core data, vendor data, search index |\n| `cd-release.yml` | CD — Release (staging + UAT) | **Manual `workflow_dispatch` only** — staging and UAT deployments are always controlled | Deploy code and data to UAT (DEV-AP01) and Staging (STG-AP01) |\n\n---\n\n### ci.yml — Continuous Integration\n\n**Triggers:** Every push to `develop`, `feature/**`, `bugfix/**`, `hotfix/**`, `release/**` branches, and every PR targeting `main` or `develop`.\n\n**Jobs:**\n\n| Job | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Lint & Unit Tests | Runs `npm run lint` and `npm run test:coverage`. Enforces 90% coverage threshold across branches, functions, lines, and statements. Publishes JUnit test results and uploads coverage report as a GitHub artifact (14-day retention). |\n\n**Key behaviour:** Fails fast on lint errors — warnings do not block the build. Coverage report is available as a downloadable artifact on every run. Uses Node.js 24 with npm cache for speed.\n\n---\n\n### pr-check.yml — Pull Request Quality Gate\n\n**Triggers:** PR opened or updated targeting `develop` or `main`.\n\n**Jobs:**\n\n| Job | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Quality Gate | Runs `npm run test:coverage`, enforces Jest coverage thresholds (90%), and posts a coverage summary comment directly on the PR. |\n\n**Key behaviour:** Blocks merge if coverage thresholds are not met. Coverage comment is updated on each new commit to the PR — no duplicate comments.\n\n---\n\n### cd-deploy.yml — Deploy to Development / SIT\n\n**Triggers:** - **Automatic:** Push to `develop` → deploys to Development (BKZK-002). - **Manual:** `workflow_dispatch` — choose target environment (`dev` or `sit`) and optionally force data or vendor data import.\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonedetect-changes\n├── lint-xml (runs if data/ or vendor/ changed)\n├── run-tests (always)\n├── deploy-code (always, needs run-tests)\n├── deploy-data (needs lint-xml + detect-changes, runs if data/core changed)\n│ └── Rebuild search index (RebuildALLSearchIndex — all sites)\n└── deploy-vendor-data (needs deploy-data, runs if data/vendor changed)\n\n**Job details:**\n\n| Job | Steps |\n| --- | --- |\n| **detect-changes** | Uses `dorny/paths-filter` to detect changes in `cartridges/`, `data/core/`, `data/vendor/`. Resolves target environment. On `workflow_dispatch` uses manually selected flags. |\n| **lint-xml** | Downloads SFCC XSD schemas, runs `node scripts/validate-xml.js` against all XML files in `data/`. Blocks `deploy-data` if any file fails schema validation. |\n| **run-tests** | Runs `npm run lint` and `npm run test`. Must pass before code is deployed. |\n| **deploy-code** | Installs vendor cartridges, zips all cartridges into a timestamped code version (`zimmermann_YYYYMMDD_HHmmss`), uploads via WebDAV, activates on the target instance. Uploads the zip as a GitHub artifact. |\n| **deploy-data** | Zips `data/core/`, uploads and imports to the target instance via `sfcc-ci instance:import`. On success, runs `sfcc-ci job:run RebuildALLSearchIndex` synchronously to rebuild product search across all 8 sites. |\n| **deploy-vendor-data** | Zips and imports `data/vendor/` (Global-e and Avalara metadata). Runs after `deploy-data`. |\n\n**Required GitHub secrets and variables:**\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client ID |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client secret |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable (env-scoped) | Sandbox hostname, e.g. `bkzk-002.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n\n---\n\n### cd-test.yml — Scheduled Test Refresh (BKZK-005)\n\n**Triggers:** - **Scheduled:** Runs automatically twice daily — **7:00 am AEST** (21:00 UTC) and **7:00 pm AEST** (09:00 UTC). - **Manual:** `workflow_dispatch` — can be triggered on demand from the GitHub Actions UI at any time.\n\n**Purpose:** Keeps the TEST environment (BKZK-005) continuously up to date with the latest code from `develop` and a clean data import, so QA always has a fresh environment. Every scheduled run performs a full refresh — code deploy, core data import, vendor data import, and search index rebuild.\n\n**Dispatch inputs (manual runs):**\n\n| Input | Description | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `deploy_data` | Import core data | true |\n| `deploy_vendor_data` | Import vendor data (Avalara, Global-e) | true |\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonelint-xml\ntest\n└── deploy-code (needs test)\n└── deploy-data (needs deploy-code + lint-xml)\n├── Rebuild search index\n└── deploy-vendor-data (needs deploy-data)\n\n**Job details:**\n\n| Job | Steps |\n| --- | --- |\n| **lint-xml** | Validates all XML files in `data/` against SFCC schemas. Blocks data import if any file fails. |\n| **test** | Runs `npm run test:coverage`. Must pass before code is deployed. |\n| **deploy-code** | Installs vendor cartridges, zips into a timestamped code version, deploys and activates on BKZK-005. |\n| **deploy-data** | Always runs on schedule. Imports `data/core/` and rebuilds the search index across all 8 sites. |\n| **deploy-vendor-data** | Always runs on schedule. Imports `data/vendor/` (Global-e and Avalara metadata) after core data. |\n\n**Required GitHub environment:** A GitHub environment named `test` with the following scoped secrets and variables:\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client ID |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OCAPI / WebDAV OAuth client secret |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable | TEST instance hostname, e.g. `bkzk-005.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com` |\n| `SFCC_CODE_VERSION_PREFIX` | Variable | Code version prefix, e.g. `zimmermann` |\n\n---\n\n### cd-release.yml — Release to UAT / Staging\n\n**Triggers:****Manual `workflow_dispatch` only.** Staging and UAT deployments are always controlled — there is no automatic push trigger. Deployments must be initiated deliberately from the GitHub Actions UI or CLI.\n\n**Dispatch inputs:**\n\n| Input | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ref` | Tag or branch to deploy, e.g. `release-1.2.3`, `release/1.2.3`, or `release/release-1.2.3` |\n| `target_environment` | `staging-and-uat` (default), `staging-only`, or `uat-only` |\n| `deploy_data` | Import core data (boolean, default false) |\n| `deploy_vendor_data` | Import vendor data (boolean, default false) |\n\n**Jobs and execution order:**\n\nnonedetect-changes + resolve-version\n├── lint-xml\n├── run-tests\n├── deploy-code-uat → deploy-code-staging\n├── deploy-data-uat → deploy-data-staging\n│ └── Rebuild search index (both UAT and Staging)\n└── deploy-vendor-data-uat → deploy-vendor-data-staging\n\n**Key differences from cd-deploy.yml:** - Extracts a release version from the provided ref (`release/1.2.3` → code version `zimmermann_release_1.2.3`). - Deploys sequentially to UAT first, then Staging — Staging is blocked until UAT succeeds. - Uses environment-scoped GitHub variables (`SFCC_INSTANCE`) to target the correct instance per stage. - Search index rebuild runs after each data import on both UAT and Staging.\n\n### Staging authentication\n\nStaging uses **certificate-based authentication** for code upload (WebDAV) and OAuth client credentials for data import (OCAPI).\n\n| Operation | Auth method | Hostname |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `code:deploy` (WebDAV) | p12 client certificate (`-c`/`-p` flags) | `cert.<SFCC_INSTANCE>` — sfcc-ci automatically adjusts to plain hostname for activation |\n| `instance:upload` (WebDAV data) | OAuth client credentials | `<SFCC_INSTANCE>` |\n| `instance:import` (OCAPI job) | OAuth client credentials | `<SFCC_INSTANCE>` |\n\n**Required secrets for the `staging` GitHub environment:**\n\n| Name | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_ID` | Secret | OAuth client ID for OCAPI (data import) |\n| `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` | Secret | OAuth client secret for OCAPI (data import) |\n| `SFCC_CODE_CERT_P12` | Secret | Base64-encoded `.p12` certificate for WebDAV code upload. Generate with: `base64 -i your-cert.p12 \\| pbcopy` |\n| `SFCC_CODE_CERT_PASSPHRASE` | Secret | Passphrase for the `.p12` certificate |\n| `SFCC_INSTANCE` | Variable | Staging hostname, e.g. `staging.yourorg.demandware.net` |\n\n---\n\n### Search index rebuild\n\nAfter every successful core data import (in `cd-deploy.yml`, `cd-test.yml`, and `cd-release.yml`), the workflow runs:\n\nbashnpx sfcc-ci job:run RebuildALLSearchIndex -i $SFCC\\_INSTANCE -s -f\n\n* **Job:**`RebuildALLSearchIndex` (defined in `data/core/jobs.xml`)\n* **Scope:**`<all-storefront-sites/>` — rebuilds product and active data search indexes for all 8 Zimmermann sites in parallel\n* **Flags:**`-s` (synchronous — waits for completion), `-f` (fail-fast — marks the workflow step as failed if the job errors)\n* **Local equivalent:**`npm run search:reindex` (also runs automatically after `npm run data:import:core` and `npm run data:import:sample`)\n\n---\n\nCI/CD tooling reference\n-----------------------\n\n| Tool / resource | Purpose | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GitHub Actions | CI/CD orchestration | Workflows in `.github/workflows/` |\n| SFCC WebDAV API | Cartridge ZIP upload | Certificate-based for staging; OAuth for dev/SIT/UAT/test |\n| OCAPI Data API | Code version management, job execution | Client credentials OAuth: `SFCC_CLIENT_ID`, `SFCC_CLIENT_SECRET` |\n| sfcc-ci (npm) | CLI wrapper for OCAPI operations | Included as a dev dependency |\n| Jest | Unit testing cartridge scripts | Mocks for `dw.*` APIs; 90% coverage threshold enforced |\n| BM (Business Manager) | Code version UI, import/export, jobs | Admin access required for production |\n| Control Center | Start/stop/create developer sandboxes | CC Admin access required |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
