      "value": "Handover details\n----------------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Outgoing architect | @Manikandan Ramachandran |\n| Incoming architect | @Victor T. Crisostomo |\n| Handover date | 2026-07-28 |\n| Project phase | Discovery / design |\n\n16falsenoneHandover detailslisttrue\n\n---\n\n1. Platform & environment access\n--------------------------------\n\n33\n135c9fad2-8ba8-414f-aa44-e94b55b17c0c\nincomplete\nSFCC Business Manager access granted for all 5 environments (dev, SIT, UAT, staging, prod) — BM URLs documented in 05.6 Environment Details\n\n34\n22f1d63a6-edab-4203-ad0d-676c5a55ea34\nincomplete\nMRT (Managed Runtime) access and environment URLs confirmed — dev, SIT, UAT, staging, prod — see 05.6 Environment Details\n\n35\n3163656c3-d67a-4f03-ab9d-31e0fb1ad301\nincomplete\nSCAPI credentials (client ID + secret) handed over for each org\n\n36\n495b787f5-91bf-44a0-817f-ee0e67f859ab\nincomplete\nGitHub repository access confirmed (zimmermann-sfcc)\n\n37\n5ababc3bd-3fd1-4c47-a807-43228a58ed20\nincomplete\nProphet Debugger access key issued for dev sandbox\n\n2. Architecture & technical design\n----------------------------------\n\n38\n3ebef163-832a-4899-9f0f-2af8f3467652\nincomplete\nHeadless architecture overview walked through (SFCC → MRT → PWA flow) — see Technical Solution Design, SFCC Build and Deployment Process\n\n39\n8abaa1e3-18b1-4c9b-ba4c-7614aece18ac\nincomplete\nCartridge path order explained for domestic vs Global-e sites — 8 sites, domestic and Global-e paths differ\n\n40\na18b8421-c64a-4c13-9b33-8b32f3eb6805\nincomplete\nCritical: Multi-site topology briefed (AU, UK, US, USIntl, EU, EUIntl, HK, ME)\n\n41\nb021ad21-9337-4be3-9642-5bbdae40ae4c\nincomplete\nMuleSoft middleware layer design explained (Exp → Process → System API)\n\n42\ne49a9e62-5796-491e-a93e-6e5bdc559ff7\nincomplete\nBM configuration management approach explained (data/core/ vs data/vendor/)\n\n---\n\n3. GitHub Actions — deployment workflow secrets\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n⚠️ The GitHub Actions deployment workflow currently uses the outgoing architect's personal MRT username and GitHub token as repository secrets. These must be rotated before the outgoing architect's access is removed.\n\n| Secret | Current state | Action required |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MRT username | Outgoing architect's personal Salesforce MRT account | Replace with a shared service account or incoming architect's credentials in GitHub repository secrets |\n| GitHub token | Outgoing architect's personal GitHub PAT (classic or fine-grained) | Generate a new PAT under the incoming architect's account (or a bot/service account) and update the secret in the repo |\n\n**Steps to rotate:**\n\n* New MRT credentials agreed — service account preferred; if personal, use incoming architect's account\n* New GitHub PAT generated with required scopes (repo, workflow minimum)\n* Both secrets updated in GitHub → repository Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions\n* Deployment workflow run validated end-to-end after rotation\n* Outgoing architect's PAT revoked once validation passes\n\n### GitHub Personal Access Tokens (PATs) in use\n\nTwo PATs are in use across the Zimmermann GitHub organisation. Both must be generated under a service account or the incoming architect's account before the outgoing architect's access is removed.\n\n| Token | Used by | Purpose | Required permissions |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `GH_ENV_READ_TOKEN` | zimmermann-pwa repository | Reads GitHub environment variables and secrets from the SFCC repo to inject into PWA build and deployment pipelines | Repository: Contents — Read · Environments — Read · Secrets — Read |\n| `ENV_SEC_RW_TOKEN` | zimmermann-sfcc-admin (cert rotation, secret management scripts) | Programmatically creates and updates GitHub repository and environment secrets — used by the SFCC cert rotation workflow and any admin automation | Repository: Secrets — Read & Write · Environments — Read & Write · Variables — Read & Write |\n\n⚠️ Both tokens must be scoped to the minimum permissions listed above. Do not use a classic PAT with broad repo scope — use fine-grained PATs targeting only the ZimmermannAU/zimmermann-sfcc repository.\n\n**Steps to rotate PATs:**\n\n* GH\\_ENV\\_READ\\_TOKEN — generate new fine-grained PAT, update secret in zimmermann-pwa repository settings\n* ENV\\_SEC\\_RW\\_TOKEN — generate new fine-grained PAT, update secret in zimmermann-sfcc repository settings\n* Validate zimmermann-pwa build pipeline can still read environment config after rotation\n* Validate cert rotation workflow can still write secrets after rotation\n* Revoke outgoing architect's PATs once all validations pass\n\n---\n\n4. Integration register & TSD walkthrough\n-----------------------------------------\n\n34 registered integrations. TSDs drafted for 8 domains — each must be walked through with the incoming architect and confirmed as read.\n\n| Vendor / system | INT-ID | Status | Handover notes & TSD |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Product catalogue** (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC) | INT-013 | Under review | AP21 is system of record. Product data flows via MuleSoft WebDAV import. Attribute taxonomy and feed cadence still open. See: TSD: Product — Catalogue & Data Integration · TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes · TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price & Inventory · TSD: Catalogue Sync — SCAPI Admin API (Alt) |\n| **Price** (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC) | INT-013 | Under review | Per-site per-currency pricebook structure. Global-e sites hold base currency only — GLE handles FX at checkout. See: TSD: Price — Pricebooks & Global-e · TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price & Inventory |\n| **Inventory** (NewStore / AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC) | INT-014 | Under review | NewStore is OMS and inventory owner. AP21 pushes DC + store stock into NewStore; NewStore exports availability to SFCC. See: TSD: Inventory — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore / AP21 · TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price & Inventory |\n| **Orders** (SFCC → MuleSoft → NewStore) | INT-014 | Under review | 3 flows: create order, order history/details, returns. SFCC sends order ID to MuleSoft; MuleSoft fetches full detail and creates in NewStore. See: TSD: Orders — SFCC ↔ MuleSoft ↔ NewStore |\n| **Tax / Avalara** (SFCC → Avalara) | INT-008 | Confirmed | Integrated via SCAPI hooks. Covers US domestic, NZ, NC, and EU domestic. All other sites use SFCC native tax tables. See: TSD: Tax — SFCC & Avalara AvaTax. Pending technical discussion with Avalara on configuration and environment setup. |\n| **Adyen** (Payments) | INT-005 | Confirmed | Salesforce Payments connector. Klarna BNPL on AU + US via Adyen connector. Cartridge present, login required. No TSD yet. Partner not engaged yet. |\n| **Global-e** (Cross-border) | INT-007 / 021 / 022 | Mixed | Checkout confirmed (007). Order sync reconciliation (021) and returns portal (022) under review. 3 separate tracked surfaces. No TSD yet. Global-e account for Zimmermann pending — only scope discussion held; technical deep dive on cartridge configuration pending. |\n| **MuleSoft** (Middleware) | INT-033 | Open questions | 25+ open questions still unresolved. Review before any integration design decisions. See: MuleSoft Integration — Open Questions for SFCC / PWA Design |\n| **Omneo** (Customer sync) | INT-023 | Under review | Bidirectional customer sync via webhooks. Option B selected — MuleSoft as integration layer. Basic profile (email, name, IDs) synced to SFCC. Addresses and marketing preferences always live from Omneo — not stored in SFCC. See: Active Customer Account Sync — Solution Options · Customer Data Migration — Solution Approach |\n| **Contentful** (CMS) | INT-002 | Under review | Headless CMS via App Exchange connector. PWA kit customisation required. Confluence page may be stale — content-type sync script exists in repo. No TSD yet. |\n| **Narvar** (Tracking / returns) | INT-018/019/020 | Under review | EDD widget (018), order tracking (019), returns redirect (020). Return status via MuleSoft → NewStore path. Initial kick-off with Narvar done; technical deep dive and API info for EDD calculation still required. No TSD yet. |\n\n⚠️ 6 integrations in the repo have no Confluence register page yet: Booxi, Transperfect, reCAPTCHA, GDPR cartridge, Optimizely, Crazy Egg.\n\n---\n\n5. Integration discovery tracker\n--------------------------------\n\nSummary of integration discovery sessions — updates discussed, gaps identified, and outstanding actions.\n\n| Third party / integration | Update | Gaps identified | Outstanding |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **MuleSoft** | Product, inventory & price sync process discussed | No current process to transform AP21 catalogue to Magento / SFCC yet | Order process is pending for discussion |\n|  | Product and inventory sample payload of AP21 → NewStore given | Inventory realtime api is missing API spec in experience API | Price book creation process flow document is pending from MuleSoft team |\n|  |  | Omneo API also required to be added to experience API | Pending product attributes transformation logic AP21 → Magento |\n| **Omneo** | Integration solution discussed | Product feeds will not be CSV from SFCC | Environment provisioning for testing |\n|  | Omneo integrated via MuleSoft — for both real-time API and data sync | MuleSoft SFCC experience API to include Omneo APIs for address | MuleSoft implementation and timeline |\n|  |  | Omneo webhook to call MuleSoft which should call SFCC |  |\n|  | Only basic customer data to be synced and stored in SFCC. Addresses read via Omneo (MuleSoft) using SCAPI hook for address |  |  |\n|  | Address update will also directly update Omneo via MuleSoft |  |  |\n|  | Marketing preferences update are via iframe |  |  |\n| **Global-e** | Global-e walked the team through the SFCC integration architecture, implementation approach, environments, jobs, pricing model, checkout flow and order lifecycle | Saved address uses traditional SFCC address book — for Zimmermann, address is directly retrieved and updated in Omneo via MuleSoft | Environment & account setup |\n|  | Zimmermann confirmed the migration is a Magento → SFCC replatform, with minimal expected changes to OMS, WMS and fulfilment processes | To minimise the impact, Omneo (via MuleSoft) should be called from SCAPI hook | Country configuration |\n| **Narvar** | Had initial kick off. API documents shared. | Could not update multiple tracking id per order. | MuleSoft discussion on Order sync mapping. Order Status mapping for SFCC — Zimmermann to provide. |\n\n---\n\n6. Open decisions & blockers\n----------------------------\n\n43\nf7d627ca-8240-40f7-a33c-18dc104d4d62\nincomplete\nMuleSoft open questions page reviewed and ownership assigned — 25+ items outstanding\n\n44\n38be9409-9cfa-46f7-ab36-632cf9bc7ad7\nincomplete\nLengow vs Feedonomics decision pending with Zimmermann — if it will be in scope or what the new approach will be\n\n45\n5b9bd8c8-78a2-47be-92ea-e663bca52ce1\nincomplete\nTSDs required for: Adyen, Global-e, Narvar — 3 missing\n\n46\n5f384ff0-3e84-4cbd-b346-6cdc4c006d05\ncomplete\nGitHub Actions deployment secrets rotated — MRT username and GitHub token off outgoing architect's personal accounts\n\n47\n22185cb8-b908-4276-9967-194cc3bfe786\nincomplete\nAccess verification to Narvar doc, Avalara, MuleSoft Anypoint exchange, MRT, SFCC env, GitHub workflow and Contentful\n\n---\n\n7. Sign-off\n-----------\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Outgoing architect sign-off |  |\n| Incoming architect sign-off |  |\n| Date completed |  |\n| Notes |  |",
